{"availability":"available","full":"AndroidPoet/rust-for-kotlin-devs","name":"rust-for-kotlin-devs","description":"A complete Rust language guide for Kotlin developers — side-by-side comparisons, idiom cheat sheet, 7-day plan, and runnable examples.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":53,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-22T10:24:16Z","updated":"2026-07-23T04:27:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://play.rust-lang.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.545Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.545Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.545Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.545Z","stars":53,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A full tour of the Rust language (roughly following The Rust Book and doc.rust-lang.org), written for someone who already knows Kotlin. Every section shows the Kotlin thing you know, then the Rust equivalent.","Runnable companion: every concept has a runnable, clippy-clean file in examples/. Clone the repo and try one: bash cargo run --example 01ownership | Example | Guide § | Example | Guide § | |---|---|---|---| | 01ownership | §10–11 | 10strings | §3 | | 02option | §5 | 11functionsclosures | §4 | | 03enumsmatch | §8–9 | 12structs | §6 | | 04result | §13 | 13derive | §7 | | 05traits | §14 | 14lifetimes | §12 | | 06iterators | §16 | 15generics | §15 | | 07async | §18 | 16modules | §17 | | 08variables | §1 | 17concurrency | §19 | | 09typestuples | §2 | | |","The 30-second summary: Rust will feel like 50% Kotlin and 50% a new way of thinking. You keep type inference, sealed-class-style enums, pattern matching, lambdas, generics, immutability-by-default, and Option/Result instead of null + exceptions. What's genuinely new: there is no garbage collector. Instead the compiler tracks ownership and borrowing of every value, and lifetimes of every reference. There is no class inheritance — you compose behavior with traits. Most of your early struggle is with the borrow checker, not the syntax. The syntax you'll learn in a day; the ownership model in a…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndroidPoet/rust-for-kotlin-devs/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"809d4ff2244f0b6321fbb7da1c6b952616e18c46a8522f777ccd0c3877308c61","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.735Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.735Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A full tour of the Rust language (roughly following The Rust Book and doc.rust-lang.org), written for someone who already knows Kotlin. Every section shows the Kotlin thing you know, then the Rust equivalent.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndroidPoet/rust-for-kotlin-devs/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"809d4ff2244f0b6321fbb7da1c6b952616e18c46a8522f777ccd0c3877308c61","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndroidPoet/rust-for-kotlin-devs/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.735Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-23T04:27:58Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndroidPoet/rust-for-kotlin-devs/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:16.737Z","hash":"809d4ff2244f0b6321fbb7da1c6b952616e18c46a8522f777ccd0c3877308c61","originalBytes":30327,"storedBytes":30327,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["rust","let","kotlin","string","mut","name","data","default","class","self","option","type","new","ownership","val","i32","cargo","like","match","shape","one","struct","trait","when","add","clone","day","impl","map","result","return","str","borrow","enums","println","shared","vec","async","copy","derive","every","list","some","debug","error","functions","generics","read","value","age","double","else","null","sealed","traits","await","both","compile","f64","int","interface","iterators","mutable","run","single","std","tokio","two","ada","enum","err","fetch","fun","hello","inheritance","lazy","max","move","n